  "representation": {
    "initialization": "Constructor prototype selection precedes message/cause/iterator effects; internal errors select their intrinsic directly, then share branded object initialization. AggregateError allocates directly with the selected prototype instead of allocating and resetting it.",
    "call": "Error calls derive the target from the active native callable and share the existing construction operation, retaining foreign prototype and realm. No added callee side map.",
    "installation": "Foreign constructor names derive from ERROR_CONSTRUCTORS. Primary/foreign prototype properties use set_named_constant, replacing a separate descriptor literal; foreign prototypes reject writes/deletion.",
    "integrity": "Functions join proxies, typed arrays and namespaces in the existing descriptor-driven TestIntegrityLevel. Queries observe the same descriptors as reflection, including virtual function metadata; no ThrowTypeError identity exception.",
    "internals": "Extended the retained root-count and weak-lifetime check to exercise explicit new targets as well as internal creation; no duplicated suite-semantic units."
  },
